From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 16:03:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: rate limit AXI errors

The EDMA misc interrupt already rate limits descriptor, SRAM, completion,
length and timeout errors. AXI read and write errors remain unbounded and
can flood the kernel log while the interrupt counters continue to provide
the exact event totals.

Apply the same net_ratelimit guard to both AXI messages. This mirrors the
targeted QSDK nss-dp correction without importing its private datapath.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma.c
@@ -346,14 +346,16 @@ static irqreturn_t edma_misc_handle_irq(
 	pr_debug("Received misc irq %d, status: %d\n", irq, misc_intr_status);
 
 	if (FIELD_GET(EDMA_MISC_AXI_RD_ERR_MASK, misc_intr_status)) {
-		pr_err("MISC AXI read error received\n");
+		if (net_ratelimit())
+			pr_err("MISC AXI read error received\n");
 		u64_stats_update_begin(&stats->syncp);
 		++stats->edma_axi_read_err;
 		u64_stats_update_end(&stats->syncp);
 	}
 
 	if (FIELD_GET(EDMA_MISC_AXI_WR_ERR_MASK, misc_intr_status)) {
-		pr_err("MISC AXI write error received\n");
+		if (net_ratelimit())
+			pr_err("MISC AXI write error received\n");
 		u64_stats_update_begin(&stats->syncp);
 		++stats->edma_axi_write_err;
 		u64_stats_update_end(&stats->syncp);
